  "description": "Reid Tract 1 | Trail mountain bike\nCapable, controlled and built for the trail – a versatile mountain bike designed to take on varied off-road terrain with confidence.\nThe Reid Tract 1 is built for riders who want to explore further and take on more challenging trails. With a rugged 6061 alloy frame, 100mm Suntour suspension fork and trail-focused components, it delivers a balanced combination of control, comfort and capability off-road.\nA Suntour coil fork with 100mm of travel helps absorb bumps and rough terrain, while the wide alloy handlebar, 70mm stem and semi-integrated headset provide a stable, responsive riding position. The 2.25\" trail tyres and double-wall alloy rims are designed to provide reliable grip and durability across varied surfaces.\nYake hydraulic disc brakes deliver controlled stopping power when riding descents or technical sections, while Shimano Altus, 16-speed gearing provides a wide range of gears for tackling climbs and changing terrain. A narrow-wide chainring helps keep the chain securely in place when the trail gets rough.\nThe Tract 1 is finished with a carefully selected range of Reid components, including lock-on grips, a trail-ready saddle, alloy seatpost and sealed bottom bracket.\nThe Tract 1 is ideal for:\n\nRiders looking to explore off-road, from local trails and bridleways to more challenging terrain\n\nTrail riding, with 100mm of front suspension and 2.25\" tyres for comfort, grip and control\n\nRiders tackling varied terrain, with Shimano Altus, 16-speed gearing for climbs, descents and changing trail conditions\n\nConfident braking on the trail, with Yake disc brakes providing controlled stopping power\n\nRiders who value stability and control, with a wide alloy handlebar and 70mm stem\n\nRegular off-road riding, with a durable 6061 alloy frame and double-wall alloy rims\n\nRiders developing their trail skills, with a capable setup designed to handle a wide range of off-road conditions",
